  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the user\'s prompt and all of its requirements. I\'m focusing on the core concept: building SkillBridge AI, an AI-powered career platform. The key features include resume analysis, skill matching with job descriptions, and identifying areas for skill improvement. I\'m taking the initial requests in the document into consideration for the development.\n\n\n**Constructing the Website\'s Foundation**\n\nI\'m now building the basic website layout using React and TypeScript, focusing on the core design elements. I\'ve opted for a clean SaaS design with a white background and indigo/violet accents. I\'m prioritizing responsiveness and have started implementing the top navigation bar with the specified elements. The landing page is taking shape with the heading, subtitle, and buttons. I\'ve also incorporated the feature cards and a simple footer. Reusable React components and clean code are central to my approach, along with Lucide icons where applicable. I\'m keeping functionality focused on navigation and button actions, leaving complex features for later stages.\n\n\n**Refining the Interface**\n\nI\'m now focused on refining the user interface to ensure it\'s responsive and maintains a clean, modern aesthetic. I\'m prioritizing a consistent color palette and clear typography, alongside intuitive navigation patterns for improved user experience. Additionally, the code documentation is underway, crucial for future scalability. I\'ve updated `metadata.json` and `index.html` to reflect the current project state, ensuring consistency across all documentation.\n\n\n**Inspecting the UI Architecture**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the UI and component structure, with a focus on the top navigation bar. I\'m prioritizing a clean SkillBridge AI logo and intuitive nav links, including Home, Dashboard, and Analyze Resume. I\'m exploring an interactive tab or scroll navigation approach that shows how the product works without a full backend. I\'m also ensuring a seamless and responsive user experience.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Navigation Functionality**\n\nI\'m making sure all navigation and button elements function as described in the requirements. I\'m focusing on a single-page layout with active navigation states and smooth anchor scrolls. For the \"Analyze Resume\" and \"Explore Features\" elements, I\'m opting for lightweight preview modals or view switchers to keep things simple. The goal is to provide a responsive and functional experience.\n\n\n**Designing Feature Cards**\n\nI\'m now designing the three feature cards with an aesthetically pleasing and spaced-out layout. I\'m focusing on the \"AI Resume Analysis,\" \"Smart Job Matching,\" and \"Personalized Learning Roadmaps\" features. I\'m incorporating Lucide icons like `FileSearch`, `Briefcase`, or `Compass`, using clear typography and a subtle \"Learn More\" call to action. I\'m aiming for a professional, zero-pill aesthetic with tabular numbers. I\'m envisioning a sample student profile display to show how SkillBridge AI works, like Priya Sharma\'s profile and match score, highlighting core strengths and missing skills.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Previews**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing interactive preview elements. For \"Analyze Resume,\" I\'m building a modal with drag-and-drop, text paste, and sample resume options, complete with a job role selector. I\'ll showcase a client-side preview, displaying analysis results like skill detection and role compatibility. For \"Dashboard,\" I\'m designing a preview that will demonstrate a student\'s learning progress and application tracker.\n\n\n"
