  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue working on the existing SkillBridge AI project. Do not rebuild the application from scratch or change the existing design.\n\nNow create the **Dashboard page**.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Keep the existing white background, indigo/violet accents, typography, and responsive design.\n2. Reuse the existing navigation bar, footer, and UI components wherever possible.\n3. Add a Dashboard page accessible through the Dashboard navigation link.\n4. Display a welcome heading: \"Welcome to Your Career Dashboard\".\n5. Add four summary cards:\n   - Total Resume Analyses\n   - Average Job Match\n   - Skills to Improve\n   - Learning Tasks Completed\n6. Add a \"Recent Analyses\" section showing example job titles, match scores, dates, and a View Details action.\n7. Add a prominent \"Analyze My Resume\" button that navigates to the resume analysis page or a placeholder page.\n8. Add a \"Quick Actions\" section with Analyze Resume, View Learning Roadmap, and Prepare for Interview.\n9. Use realistic sample data only for the dashboard preview. Clearly keep it separate from real user data.\n10. Make all navigation links and buttons work wherever their target pages exist.\n11. Ensure the dashboard works on desktop and mobile.\n12. Do not add authentication, a database, or AI functionality yet.\n\nKeep the code clean and reusable. Preserve all existing working functionality and make sure the application runs without errors."
    items {
      text: "Continue working on the existing SkillBridge AI project. Do not rebuild the application from scratch or change the existing design.\n\nNow create the **Dashboard page**.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Keep the existing white background, indigo/violet accents, typography, and responsive design.\n2. Reuse the existing navigation bar, footer, and UI components wherever possible.\n3. Add a Dashboard page accessible through the Dashboard navigation link.\n4. Display a welcome heading: \"Welcome to Your Career Dashboard\".\n5. Add four summary cards:\n   - Total Resume Analyses\n   - Average Job Match\n   - Skills to Improve\n   - Learning Tasks Completed\n6. Add a \"Recent Analyses\" section showing example job titles, match scores, dates, and a View Details action.\n7. Add a prominent \"Analyze My Resume\" button that navigates to the resume analysis page or a placeholder page.\n8. Add a \"Quick Actions\" section with Analyze Resume, View Learning Roadmap, and Prepare for Interview.\n9. Use realistic sample data only for the dashboard preview. Clearly keep it separate from real user data.\n10. Make all navigation links and buttons work wherever their target pages exist.\n11. Ensure the dashboard works on desktop and mobile.\n12. Do not add authentication, a database, or AI functionality yet.\n\nKeep the code clean and reusable. Preserve all existing working functionality and make sure the application runs without errors."
    }
  }
}
