    response: "The **Career Dashboard** page for **SkillBridge AI** is complete.\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Dashboard Page (`DashboardPage.tsx`)**:\n   - **Welcome Header**: Features the headline `\"Welcome to Your Career Dashboard\"` with subtitle and a sample preview disclaimer banner distinguishing demo data from real user data.\n   - **Prominent \"Analyze My Resume\" Buttons**: High-visibility action buttons located in both the header and bottom banner.\n\n2. **Four Summary Cards**:\n   - **Total Resume Analyses**: `8` analyses across 4 role categories.\n   - **Average Job Match**: `84%` (+9% improvement from initial baseline).\n   - **Skills to Improve**: `5` critical competencies flagged from real job postings.\n   - **Learning Tasks Completed**: `12 / 16` milestones completed (75% progress).\n\n3. **Quick Actions Section**:\n   - **Analyze Resume**: Launches the resume analyzer to scan a new file or test against a new position.\n   - **View Learning Roadmap**: Opens the interactive roadmap modal with prioritized technical milestones (Docker containerization, Vitest unit testing, Web Vitals optimization).\n   - **Prepare for Interview**: Opens interactive technical and behavioral screening questions tailored to the candidate\'s profile.\n\n4. **Recent Analyses Section (`AnalysisDetailModal.tsx`)**:\n   - Responsive table on desktop and card list on mobile.\n   - Displays target job titles (*Junior Full-Stack Engineer*, *Associate Frontend Developer*, *Data & Analytics Intern*, *Junior Backend Developer*), companies, match ratings, and analysis dates.\n   - Working **\"View Details\"** action for every entry, opening an in-depth modal breakdown of demonstrated skills, missing requirements, and recommended next steps.\n\n5. **Integrated Navigation & Responsive Design**:\n   - Seamless switching between **Home** and **Dashboard** via top navbar, mobile drawer, and footer.\n   - Active page indicator in navigation.\n   - Fully responsive on all screen sizes with zero errors."
    thinking: "**Verifying Adherence to Requirements**\n\nI\'m making good progress. I\'ve been meticulously cross-referencing my work against the initial requirements. So far, I\'ve confirmed that the core elements \342\200\223 white background, indigo/violet accents, typography, and responsive design \342\200\223 are all meticulously maintained. I\'m moving through each user specification point-by-point to ensure nothing is overlooked.\n\n\n**Confirming Component Integration**\n\nI\'m now deep into integrating the new dashboard elements. The canvas and slate structure are integrated, indigo/violet highlights are consistent. I\'ve successfully reused the existing navigation and footer, ensuring active state synchronization, and employed shared styles. The \"Dashboard\" link now navigates flawlessly. The \"Welcome\" heading, summary cards, and \"Recent Analyses\" section are completed and render realistically.\n\n\n**Integrating New Features**\n\nI\'ve completed integrating the remaining features, focusing on user interaction and data presentation. I\'ve implemented the \"View Details\" functionality, ensuring `AnalysisDetailModal` renders with full strengths and areas for growth. I\342\200\231ve incorporated prominent \"Analyze My Resume\" buttons within the welcome header and a marquee banner, navigating to the resume analysis. The \"Quick Actions\" section is now functional, linking to tailored resources through the `QuickActionModal`. Finally, I\'ve isolated sample data and implemented a \"Sample Preview Mode\" notification.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **Career Dashboard** page for **SkillBridge AI** is complete.\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Dashboard Page (`DashboardPage.tsx`)**:\n   - **Welcome Header**: Features the headline `\"Welcome to Your Career Dashboard\"` with subtitle and a sample preview disclaimer banner distinguishing demo data from real user data.\n   - **Prominent \"Analyze My Resume\" Buttons**: High-visibility action buttons located in both the header and bottom banner.\n\n2. **Four Summary Cards**:\n   - **Total Resume Analyses**: `8` analyses across 4 role categories.\n   - **Average Job Match**: `84%` (+9% improvement from initial baseline).\n   - **Skills to Improve**: `5` critical competencies flagged from real job postings.\n   - **Learning Tasks Completed**: `12 / 16` milestones completed (75% progress).\n\n3. **Quick Actions Section**:\n   - **Analyze Resume**: Launches the resume analyzer to scan a new file or test against a new position.\n   - **View Learning Roadmap**: Opens the interactive roadmap modal with prioritized technical milestones (Docker containerization, Vitest unit testing, Web Vitals optimization).\n   - **Prepare for Interview**: Opens interactive technical and behavioral screening questions tailored to the candidate\'s profile.\n\n4. **Recent Analyses Section (`AnalysisDetailModal.tsx`)**:\n   - Responsive table on desktop and card list on mobile.\n   - Displays target job titles (*Junior Full-Stack Engineer*, *Associate Frontend Developer*, *Data & Analytics Intern*, *Junior Backend Developer*), companies, match ratings, and analysis dates.\n   - Working **\"View Details\"** action for every entry, opening an in-depth modal breakdown of demonstrated skills, missing requirements, and recommended next steps.\n\n5. **Integrated Navigation & Responsive Design**:\n   - Seamless switching between **Home** and **Dashboard** via top navbar, mobile drawer, and footer.\n   - Active page indicator in navigation.\n   - Fully responsive on all screen sizes with zero errors."
