  user_input {
    user_response: "Continue developing the existing SkillBridge AI project. Do not rebuild the application from scratch or modify the existing landing page and dashboard unnecessarily.\n\nNow create the **Resume Analysis page**.\n\n### 1. Page design\n- Follow the existing white, indigo, and violet design.\n- Add the heading \"Analyze Your Career Fit\".\n- Add a subtitle: \"Discover how your skills align with your dream role.\"\n- Keep the existing navigation and responsive layout.\n\n### 2. Resume upload section\n- Create a drag-and-drop resume upload area.\n- Accept PDF files only.\n- Display the uploaded filename and file size.\n- Provide a button to remove the uploaded file.\n- Validate the file type and show a helpful error for invalid files.\n- Also provide a text area where users can paste resume text instead of uploading a PDF.\n- Require at least one resume input: uploaded PDF or pasted text.\n\n### 3. Job description section\n- Add a large text area labeled \"Paste Job Description\".\n- Include a helpful placeholder with an example job description.\n- Validate that the job description is not empty.\n\n### 4. Analyze button\n- Add a prominent \"Analyze My Match\" button.\n- Disable the button when the required inputs are missing.\n- Show a loading indicator when the form is submitted.\n- For now, do not generate fake AI results or claim that a real analysis has happened.\n- After valid submission, show a clear temporary message explaining that the analysis engine will be connected in the next development step.\n\n### 5. User experience\n- Show clear validation errors.\n- Add a short privacy notice explaining that uploaded resumes may contain personal information.\n- Make the page responsive on mobile and desktop.\n- Reuse existing components and styling.\n- Keep the code clean and maintainable.\n\n### Important\nDo not implement Gemini API integration, resume parsing, database storage, or authentication yet. Focus only on the resume input form and its frontend interactions.\n\nPreserve the existing landing page and dashboard. Ensure all pages still work without errors."
    items {
      text: "Continue developing the existing SkillBridge AI project. Do not rebuild the application from scratch or modify the existing landing page and dashboard unnecessarily.\n\nNow create the **Resume Analysis page**.\n\n### 1. Page design\n- Follow the existing white, indigo, and violet design.\n- Add the heading \"Analyze Your Career Fit\".\n- Add a subtitle: \"Discover how your skills align with your dream role.\"\n- Keep the existing navigation and responsive layout.\n\n### 2. Resume upload section\n- Create a drag-and-drop resume upload area.\n- Accept PDF files only.\n- Display the uploaded filename and file size.\n- Provide a button to remove the uploaded file.\n- Validate the file type and show a helpful error for invalid files.\n- Also provide a text area where users can paste resume text instead of uploading a PDF.\n- Require at least one resume input: uploaded PDF or pasted text.\n\n### 3. Job description section\n- Add a large text area labeled \"Paste Job Description\".\n- Include a helpful placeholder with an example job description.\n- Validate that the job description is not empty.\n\n### 4. Analyze button\n- Add a prominent \"Analyze My Match\" button.\n- Disable the button when the required inputs are missing.\n- Show a loading indicator when the form is submitted.\n- For now, do not generate fake AI results or claim that a real analysis has happened.\n- After valid submission, show a clear temporary message explaining that the analysis engine will be connected in the next development step.\n\n### 5. User experience\n- Show clear validation errors.\n- Add a short privacy notice explaining that uploaded resumes may contain personal information.\n- Make the page responsive on mobile and desktop.\n- Reuse existing components and styling.\n- Keep the code clean and maintainable.\n\n### Important\nDo not implement Gemini API integration, resume parsing, database storage, or authentication yet. Focus only on the resume input form and its frontend interactions.\n\nPreserve the existing landing page and dashboard. Ensure all pages still work without errors."
    }
  }
}
