  planner_response {
    response: "The **Resume Analysis page** for **SkillBridge AI** is now built and integrated into the application.\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Page Design & Header (`ResumeAnalysisPage.tsx`)**:\n   - **Heading**: `\"Analyze Your Career Fit\"`\n   - **Subtitle**: `\"Discover how your skills align with your dream role.\"`\n   - Maintained the clean white aesthetic with crisp borders and indigo/violet accents.\n\n2. **Resume Input Section**:\n   - **Drag & Drop Upload Area**:\n     - Accepts **PDF files only** with drag-and-drop and manual file browse support.\n     - Displays the uploaded file name, formatted file size (KB/MB), and a green verification badge.\n     - Includes a remove button (`X`) to clear or swap the uploaded file.\n     - Validates the file format and displays clear inline error messages for invalid formats (e.g. non-PDF uploads).\n   - **Pasted Text Alternative**:\n     - Toggle between **Upload PDF** and **Paste Text** modes.\n     - Provides a large text area with live character counting.\n     - Includes a 1-click **\"Use Sample Student Resume\"** helper for immediate testing.\n   - **Validation**: Requires either an uploaded PDF or pasted resume text.\n\n3. **Job Description Section**:\n   - Large text area with a realistic example placeholder.\n   - **\"Insert Sample Job\"** quick action button to auto-fill a sample *Junior Full-Stack Developer* posting.\n   - Full validation ensuring the job description is not blank.\n\n4. **\"Analyze My Match\" Button & Staging Confirmation**:\n   - Prominent action button that is disabled until valid resume input and a job description are provided.\n   - Displays an animated loading spinner during submission.\n   - Displays a clean confirmation status message stating:\n     > *\"Your inputs have been verified and structured. The AI analysis engine will be connected in the next development step to perform deep semantic skill extraction, ATS keyword matching, and personalized learning roadmap generation.\"*\n   - Includes quick action links to edit inputs or jump directly to the **Career Dashboard**.\n\n5. **User Experience & Privacy**:\n   - **Privacy Notice**: Explains that uploaded resumes may contain personal contact details and that all processing in this stage remains securely client-side in the user\'s browser.\n   - **Fully Responsive**: Adapts seamlessly across desktop, tablet, and mobile screen sizes.\n\n6. **Unified Navigation**:\n   - The top navigation bar, mobile menu, and footer now smoothly route between **Home**, **Dashboard**, and **Analyze Resume** with active link indicators."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Requirements Thoroughly**\n\nOkay, I\'m meticulously reviewing the user\'s requirements now, going point by point to ensure I haven\'t overlooked anything. The existing design elements of white, indigo, and violet are confirmed, and the heading \"Analyze Your Career Fit\" is also noted. I\'m focusing on the specifics for each component to make sure they\'re right.\n\n\n**Confirming Specific Features**\n\nI\'ve just confirmed the subtitle matches precisely. The existing navigation and responsive layout are fully synchronized. The resume upload section is designed: a drag-and-drop area with the correct drag states, accepting PDFs validated by file type and extension. Uploaded filename, file size, and remove button are implemented. Finally, there\'s the necessary validation with a useful error message and the functionality to accept text pasted from a resume is seamless.\n\n\n**Adding Input Verification**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the user input validation. The design will feature toggling between \"Upload PDF\" and \"Paste Text\", including a character counter and a sample text inserter. The system will require at least one resume input, validating this before form submission. The job description section will have a large text area labeled \"Target Job Description,\" with a sample placeholder. A validation will confirm this field is not empty. Finally, the \"Analyze My Match\" button will be disabled, with an opacity change and cursor style update, until all required fields are filled. A loading spinner will display during form submission.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The **Resume Analysis page** for **SkillBridge AI** is now built and integrated into the application.\n\n### What Was Built:\n\n1. **Page Design & Header (`ResumeAnalysisPage.tsx`)**:\n   - **Heading**: `\"Analyze Your Career Fit\"`\n   - **Subtitle**: `\"Discover how your skills align with your dream role.\"`\n   - Maintained the clean white aesthetic with crisp borders and indigo/violet accents.\n\n2. **Resume Input Section**:\n   - **Drag & Drop Upload Area**:\n     - Accepts **PDF files only** with drag-and-drop and manual file browse support.\n     - Displays the uploaded file name, formatted file size (KB/MB), and a green verification badge.\n     - Includes a remove button (`X`) to clear or swap the uploaded file.\n     - Validates the file format and displays clear inline error messages for invalid formats (e.g. non-PDF uploads).\n   - **Pasted Text Alternative**:\n     - Toggle between **Upload PDF** and **Paste Text** modes.\n     - Provides a large text area with live character counting.\n     - Includes a 1-click **\"Use Sample Student Resume\"** helper for immediate testing.\n   - **Validation**: Requires either an uploaded PDF or pasted resume text.\n\n3. **Job Description Section**:\n   - Large text area with a realistic example placeholder.\n   - **\"Insert Sample Job\"** quick action button to auto-fill a sample *Junior Full-Stack Developer* posting.\n   - Full validation ensuring the job description is not blank.\n\n4. **\"Analyze My Match\" Button & Staging Confirmation**:\n   - Prominent action button that is disabled until valid resume input and a job description are provided.\n   - Displays an animated loading spinner during submission.\n   - Displays a clean confirmation status message stating:\n     > *\"Your inputs have been verified and structured. The AI analysis engine will be connected in the next development step to perform deep semantic skill extraction, ATS keyword matching, and personalized learning roadmap generation.\"*\n   - Includes quick action links to edit inputs or jump directly to the **Career Dashboard**.\n\n5. **User Experience & Privacy**:\n   - **Privacy Notice**: Explains that uploaded resumes may contain personal contact details and that all processing in this stage remains securely client-side in the user\'s browser.\n   - **Fully Responsive**: Adapts seamlessly across desktop, tablet, and mobile screen sizes.\n\n6. **Unified Navigation**:\n   - The top navigation bar, mobile menu, and footer now smoothly route between **Home**, **Dashboard**, and **Analyze Resume** with active link indicators."
