  user_input {
    user_response: "Fix the existing SkillBridge AI project. The Resume Analysis form currently displays this message after submission:\n\n\"Resume and Job Description Received \342\200\224 Form Staged. The analysis engine will be connected in the next development step.\"\n\nThis is not the expected behavior. I need actual AI evaluation now.\n\nPlease inspect the existing code and identify the exact form submission handler and any placeholder logic responsible for displaying this message.\n\nImplement the following:\n\n1. Remove the placeholder \"Form Staged\" success flow and connect the existing \"Analyze My Match\" button to a real asynchronous Gemini API analysis function.\n\n2. Ensure the submitted resume and job description are actually passed to the analysis function.\n\n3. For PDF uploads, extract the resume text first. If extraction fails, show a clear error rather than claiming the resume was analyzed.\n\n4. Support pasted resume text as an alternative to PDF uploads.\n\n5. Call Gemini using the supported SDK and the project\'s configured secure API-key mechanism. Never expose secrets in browser code or hardcode API keys.\n\n6. Ask Gemini to return structured JSON containing:\n   - matchScore (0\342\200\223100)\n   - matchedSkills\n   - missingSkills\n   - resumeEvidence\n   - recommendations\n   - learningRoadmap\n   - interviewQuestions\n\n7. Parse and validate the returned data, then display the actual results on the results page. Do not display placeholder scores or sample results as real analysis.\n\n8. Add a loading indicator while the request runs, and handle missing API configuration, API quota limits, network errors, and invalid AI responses.\n\n9. Preserve the existing UI, landing page, dashboard, and navigation. Do not rebuild the application.\n\n10. After implementing the fix, verify that clicking \"Analyze My Match\" calls the real AI function rather than displaying the old staged message. Tell me exactly which configuration steps, if any, I must complete manually.\n\nMake the necessary code changes now, not just a plan or explanation."
    items {
      text: "Fix the existing SkillBridge AI project. The Resume Analysis form currently displays this message after submission:\n\n\"Resume and Job Description Received \342\200\224 Form Staged. The analysis engine will be connected in the next development step.\"\n\nThis is not the expected behavior. I need actual AI evaluation now.\n\nPlease inspect the existing code and identify the exact form submission handler and any placeholder logic responsible for displaying this message.\n\nImplement the following:\n\n1. Remove the placeholder \"Form Staged\" success flow and connect the existing \"Analyze My Match\" button to a real asynchronous Gemini API analysis function.\n\n2. Ensure the submitted resume and job description are actually passed to the analysis function.\n\n3. For PDF uploads, extract the resume text first. If extraction fails, show a clear error rather than claiming the resume was analyzed.\n\n4. Support pasted resume text as an alternative to PDF uploads.\n\n5. Call Gemini using the supported SDK and the project\'s configured secure API-key mechanism. Never expose secrets in browser code or hardcode API keys.\n\n6. Ask Gemini to return structured JSON containing:\n   - matchScore (0\342\200\223100)\n   - matchedSkills\n   - missingSkills\n   - resumeEvidence\n   - recommendations\n   - learningRoadmap\n   - interviewQuestions\n\n7. Parse and validate the returned data, then display the actual results on the results page. Do not display placeholder scores or sample results as real analysis.\n\n8. Add a loading indicator while the request runs, and handle missing API configuration, API quota limits, network errors, and invalid AI responses.\n\n9. Preserve the existing UI, landing page, dashboard, and navigation. Do not rebuild the application.\n\n10. After implementing the fix, verify that clicking \"Analyze My Match\" calls the real AI function rather than displaying the old staged message. Tell me exactly which configuration steps, if any, I must complete manually.\n\nMake the necessary code changes now, not just a plan or explanation."
    }
  }
}
