  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Backend Setup**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the `package.json` file alongside the backend instructions. Specifically, I am focusing on the `server.ts` entry point and the integration with Express and `vite.middlewares` in development.\n\n\n**Analyzing Key Management**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to deployment and API key security. I\'ve noted that the API key is server-only, accessed via `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`, and never sent to the browser, with no UI elements for key input or management. The application will never request the API key from the user.\n\n\n**Investigating Package Options**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of PDF text extraction. I\'m focusing on whether this can be handled in the browser or if server-side processing is necessary. I\'m exploring the feasibility of using packages like `pdfjs-dist` and `pdf-parse`, and considering how to manage package installations with the available tools.\n\n\n**Evaluating PDF Handling**\n\nI\'ve been exploring PDF text extraction options. I\'m focusing on text extraction from PDF uploads, aiming to address the requirement to handle failed extractions gracefully. I\'m now examining the use of `pdfjs-dist` on the client-side or `pdf-parse` on the server-side, considering their compatibility and implementation complexity. The goal is to support text extraction from PDFs, given the explicit requirement.\n\n\n**Assessing Text Extraction Approaches**\n\nI\'m now investigating PDF text extraction methods further. I\'m focusing on whether `pdf-parse` can be directly integrated and whether any build or node version complications arise. I\'m also considering client-side PDF text extraction using `pdfjs-dist` and server-side processing, checking for compatibility and potential issues with Vite or bundlers in production. My focus now is on confirming the viability of `pdf-parse` or `pdfjs-dist` installations. I\'m also planning fallback strategies if text extraction fails. I\'m considering sending text or base64 data to the server, and extract the PDF data there, to ensure extraction happens even with a blank text resume.\n\n\n"
