    thinking: "**Verifying Server Setup**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started examining the server setup guidelines within the framework documentation. My focus is on ensuring alignment with the required `server.ts` entry point running Express and integration of `vite.middlewares`. I am verifying the current setup\'s adherence to the Express-Vite integration specified in the system prompt to determine if backend routes are needed.\n\n\n**Confirming API Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Gemini API, focusing on the server-side utility for the client, and ensuring the `User-Agent` header is correctly set to \"aistudio-build\". I\'m using `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` for API key access and confirming that the server is configured to prevent it from ever reaching the browser. I\'ve also verified the default model is \'gemini-3.8-flash\'.\n\n\n**Defining Gemini Schema**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining a rigorous JSON schema for Gemini, based on the requirements for structured data. I\'m carefully detailing each field, including `matchScore`, `matchedSkills` (with detailed object structure: `skill`, `category`, `context`), `missingSkills`, `resumeEvidence`, `recommendations`, `learningRoadmap`, and `interviewQuestions`. I aim to ensure complete schema compliance to ensure accurate parsing and validation for the results page.\n\n\n**Elaborating Structured Data**\n\nI\'m currently fleshing out the structured data within the Gemini schema. I\'m focusing on \"resumeEvidence,\" \"recommendations,\" \"learningRoadmap,\" and \"interviewQuestions.\" I\'m populating these fields with example data. I\'m especially focused on providing specific and useful items, like suggesting a Docker learning path with clear actions and resources. I\'m also ensuring the \"interviewQuestions\" field includes relevant topics.\n\n\n**Refining Data Structures**\n\nI\'m now refining the Gemini schema to enhance its flexibility and error handling. I\'m focusing on ensuring graceful handling of different data types for `matchedSkills`, `missingSkills`, `resumeEvidence`, `recommendations`, `learningRoadmap`, and `interviewQuestions`. I\'m allowing for either strings or objects (or array thereof) for each field. I\'m prioritizing compatibility, so the frontend can handle mixed data types without runtime crashes. I\'m checking the `@google/genai` library\'s `Type` enum to assist in this process.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust error handling for the API endpoint, focusing on returning informative JSON responses for various failure scenarios. I\'m accounting for missing API keys (500/503), PDF extraction failures (400), rate limiting (429), and network/AI response issues (500/502). I\'m checking the `package.json` file for the `dev` script to check how Express and Vite are currently mounted.\n\n\n**Analyzing Server Build Scripts**\n\nI\'m now examining the `package.json` file\'s scripts, specifically `\"build\"` and `\"start\"`, to align with the framework guidelines. I\'m noting the absence of a `start` script, which will be `\"start\": \"node server.ts\"`, as per the documentation. I\'m checking that the `\"dev\"` script correctly mounts `vite.middlewares` by running `tsx server.ts`. I am noting that the current `clean` script cleans the dist and generated `server.js` file.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Vite Integration**\n\nI\'m now focusing on verifying the Vite integration within the server. I\'ve re-examined the code, confirming Vite\'s middleware is correctly mounted in development mode, while production serves static assets. I\'m confirming that the `vite.config.ts` setup properly configures the Vite build to work correctly in the deployed Express environment.\n\n\n"
