  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Configuration and Metadata**\n\nI\'ve examined the `vite.config.ts` file; it\'s a standard Vite setup, incorporating Tailwind CSS via `@tailwindcss/vite` and React with `@vitejs/plugin-react`. Next, I looked at `metadata.json`. The key pieces I noted there are the project name \"SkillBridge AI\" and its description focusing on AI-powered career assistance.\n\n\n**Investigating pdf-parse Implementation**\n\nI\'m now focused on integrating `pdf-parse`. I\'m testing its import in TypeScript/Node to ensure compatibility, especially regarding ES Modules and potential CommonJS issues. I\'m looking at different import strategies and checking the type definitions to ensure everything works correctly with `tsc --noEmit`. I\'m also confirming the function signature: `pdf-parse(buffer: Buffer): Promise<{ text: string, numpages: number, ... }>`.\n\n\n**Implementing Gemini Integration**\n\nMy current task is to connect the \"Analyze My Match\" button to an asynchronous Gemini API analysis function. I must ensure the resume and job description are passed correctly. I\'m focusing on text extraction from PDF uploads first. I need to handle potential failures gracefully, showing a clear error. I will then support pasted resume text, and use a secure API key integration. I need to make sure I am receiving and validating the output.\n\n\n**Refining Result Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on displaying the actual analysis results, not placeholders. I\'ll be parsing and validating the returned data, then integrating it into the results page in place of the staged message. The \"Resume and Job Description Received \342\200\224 Form Staged\" message is gone! The goal is a comprehensive, professional results section with an \"Overall Match Score\" circular gauge.\n\n\n**Designing Result Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the result display details. I\'m thinking of using color-coding for alignment scores: 80-100% is High, 60-79% is Moderate, and below 60% is Developing. I need to display \"Matched Skills\" as tags with context. \"Missing Skills\" should highlight gaps. \"Resume Evidence\" will be concrete claims from the resume. I\'m also planning actionable recommendations, a personalized learning roadmap, and tailored interview questions. I need action buttons, of course.\n\n\n**Adding Action Buttons**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating action buttons! \"Analyze Another Resume\" resets the form for a new scan, and \"Save to Dashboard\" lets users add the real analysis to their career dashboard. I can store this analysis in state and have it appear under \"Recent Analyses.\" I\'m also planning \"Print / Export Report\" and \"Copy Analysis Summary\" options.\n\nLet\'s design the `server.ts` endpoint!\n\n\n**Crafting Endpoint Logic**\n\nI\'m now writing the logic for the `server.ts` endpoint, focusing on PDF text extraction using `pdf-parse` and handling various input scenarios. I\'m prioritizing error handling; I\'m making sure that empty PDFs, scanned PDFs, or missing API keys provide clear, informative errors. I\'m setting up to use either the uploaded PDF text or the pasted resume text. Next, I\'ll integrate the Gemini API call.\n\n\n**Defining Gemini Request**\n\nI\'m now composing the prompt for the Gemini API call. It\'s designed for a rigorous, honest evaluation, comparing the resume to the job description. I\'m focusing on identifying true competencies, critical missing qualifications, and providing actionable guidance. I\'ve configured it to request a JSON response, adhering to a predefined schema for consistent data processing. The prompt will be generated, combining the final resume text and the job description.\n\n\n**Defining Data Structure**\n\nI\'m now defining the data structure for missing skills in the JSON response from the Gemini API. Each missing skill will contain the skill itself, its priority (High, Medium, or Low), and a clear reason for its importance. The overall goal is to provide actionable insights for users.\n\n\n**Structuring JSON Results**\n\nI\'m solidifying the structure for the JSON response now. I am also working on `resumeEvidence`, which will include claims and the specific supporting evidence. I am also setting up recommendations and milestones for the learning roadmap.\n\n\n**Refining Response Format**\n\nI\'m now refining the JSON response schema. I\'m focusing on the `learningRoadmap` and `interviewQuestions` sections. I am structuring the `learningRoadmap` to contain milestones, timeframes, and action items. Interview questions will be categorized by topic and specify the expected focus, ensuring comprehensive preparation for users. I am also working on adding detailed validation to the structure.\n\n\n**Implementing Error Handling**\n\nI\'m now implementing robust error handling for the Gemini API calls, focusing on specific error codes. I\'ll provide informative messages for rate limits (`429`), invalid requests (`400`), and network failures (`502`). All JSON parsing issues will trigger a fallback or explicit error. I also added `extractedResumeLength` to the HTTP 200 response. Next, I will review the `package.json` scripts.\n\n```json\n\"scripts\": {\n  \"dev\": \"vite --port=3000 --host=0.0.0.0\",\n  \"build\": \"vite build\",\n  \"preview\": \"vite preview\",\n  \"clean\": \"rm -rf dist server.js\",\n  \"lint\": \"tsc --noEmit\"\n}\n```\n\n\n**Updating Package Scripts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the `package.json` scripts, specifically the \"dev\" and \"start\" commands. I\'m updating \"dev\" to use \"tsx server.ts\" for development and then also updating the \"start\" script to use \"tsx server.ts\" or \"node --import tsx server.ts\" or even just \"node dist-server/server.js\", which are all now valid. I think \"tsx server.ts\" is the best for consistency. I am also planning to review the server.ts code.\n\nI\'m also working on `pdf-parse`. I\'ll verify the direct import works with tsx.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_128115"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"CodeContent\":\"import express from \'express\';\\nimport dotenv from \'dotenv\';\\nimport path from \'path\';\\nimport { fileURLToPath } from \'url\';\\nimport { GoogleGenAI, Type } from \'@google/genai\';\\n// @ts-ignore\\nimport pdfParse from \'pdf-parse\';\\n\\ndotenv.config();\\n\\nconst __filename = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url);\\nconst __dirname = path.dirname(__filename);\\n\\nconst app = express();\\nconst port = process.env.PORT || 3000;\\n\\n// Allow payloads up to 15MB for PDF base64 handling\\napp.use(express.json({ limit: \'15mb\' }));\\n\\n// Helper function to safely extract text from PDF buffer\\nasync function extractTextFromPdf(buffer: Buffer): Promise<string> {\\n  try {\\n    const parsePdf = (pdfParse as any).default || pdfParse;\\n    const data = await parsePdf(buffer);\\n    const text = data?.text?.trim() || \'\';\\n    return text;\\n  } catch (error: any) {\\n    console.error(\'PDF parsing error:\', error);\\n    throw new Error(\'Failed to parse PDF document.\');\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n// POST endpoint for resume analysis using real Gemini API\\napp.post(\'/api/analyze-resume\', async (req, res) => {\\n  try {\\n    const { resumePdfBase64, resumePdfName, resumeText, jobDescription } = req.body;\\n\\n    // Validate job description\\n    if (!jobDescription || typeof jobDescription !== \'string\' || jobDescription.trim().length < 15) {\\n      return res.status(400).json({\\n        error: \'Please provide a valid job description (at least 15 characters).\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    let finalResumeText = \'\';\\n\\n    // If PDF upload is provided, extract text from it first\\n    if (resumePdfBase64) {\\n      try {\\n        const base64Data = resumePdfBase64.replace(/^data:application\\\\/pdf;base64,/, \'\');\\n        const pdfBuffer = Buffer.from(base64Data, \'base64\');\\n        const extractedText = await extractTextFromPdf(pdfBuffer);\\n\\n        if (!extractedText || extractedText.length < 30) {\\n          return res.status(400).json({\\n            error:\\n              \'Unable to extract readable text from the uploaded PDF. The file may be a scanned image without an OCR text layer or password-protected. Please upload a text-based PDF or paste your resume text directly.\',\\n          });\\n        }\\n\\n        finalResumeText = extractedText;\\n      } catch (err: any) {\\n        return res.status(400).json({\\n          error:\\n            \'Unable to process the uploaded PDF file. Please ensure it is a valid, uncorrupted PDF document or paste your resume text.\',\\n        });\\n      }\\n    } else if (resumeText && typeof resumeText === \'string\' && resumeText.trim().length >= 20) {\\n      // Pasted resume text alternative\\n      finalResumeText = resumeText.trim();\\n    } else {\\n      return res.status(400).json({\\n        error: \'Please provide your resume by uploading a PDF or pasting the resume text.\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    // Check Gemini API key configuration\\n    const apiKey = process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY;\\n    if (!apiKey || apiKey === \'MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\' || apiKey.trim() === \'\') {\\n      return res.status(503).json({\\n        error:\\n          \'GEMINI_API_KEY is not configured on the server. Please add your Gemini API key in the AI Studio Settings > Secrets panel (or in your .env file).\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    // Initialize GoogleGenAI SDK with user agent telemetry\\n    const ai = new GoogleGenAI({\\n      apiKey,\\n      httpOptions: {\\n        headers: {\\n          \'User-Agent\': \'aistudio-build\',\\n        },\\n      },\\n    });\\n\\n    const systemInstruction = `You are a senior technical hiring manager and career advisor.\\nYour job is to rigorously, honestly, and constructively evaluate a candidate\'s actual resume against a target job description.\\nFollow these rules strictly:\\n1. Ground all analysis strictly in the provided candidate resume text and target job description. Never hallucinate skills or work experiences that are not present.\\n2. Calculate a realistic matchScore between 0 and 100 based on core requirements overlap (e.g. required vs nice-to-have, years of experience, relevant tech stack).\\n3. Identify true matchedSkills (with context showing where in the resume it was found) and critical missingSkills (with priority and hiring importance).\\n4. Extract specific resumeEvidence claims directly from their projects or work bullets.\\n5. Provide high-impact recommendations to improve the resume for this position.\\n6. Generate a targeted, realistic learningRoadmap to bridge missing qualifications.\\n7. Provide custom interviewQuestions tailored directly to the candidate\'s actual resume projects and potential weak spots.\\nReturn structured JSON only matching the schema.`;\\n\\n    const userPrompt = `Please evaluate the following candidate resume against the target job description:\\n\\n=== CANDIDATE RESUME ===\\n${finalResumeText}\\n\\n=== TARGET JOB DESCRIPTION ===\\n${jobDescription.trim()}`;\\n\\n    // Call Gemini 3.8 Flash with structured JSON schema\\n    const response = await ai.models.generateContent({\\n      model: \'gemini-3.8-flash\',\\n      contents: userPrompt,\\n      config: {\\n        systemInstruction,\\n        temperature: 0.3,\\n        responseMimeType: \'application/json\',\\n        responseSchema: {\\n          type: Type.OBJECT,\\n          properties: {\\n            matchScore: {\\n              type: Type.INTEGER,\\n              description: \'Overall job compatibility score between 0 and 100.\',\\n            },\\n            matchedSkills: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  skill: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  category: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  context: {\\n                    type: Type.STRING,\\n                    description: \'Where or how this skill was evidenced in the resume.\',\\n                  },\\n                },\\n                required: [\'skill\', \'category\', \'context\'],\\n              },\\n              description: \'Competencies evidenced in the resume matching the job.\',\\n            },\\n            missingSkills: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  skill: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  priority: { type: Type.STRING, description: \'High, Medium, or Low\' },\\n                  reason: { type: Type.STRING, description: \'Why this is critical for the job.\' },\\n                },\\n                required: [\'skill\', \'priority\', \'reason\'],\\n              },\\n              description: \'Key requirements in the job description missing from the resume.\',\\n            },\\n            resumeEvidence: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  claim: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  evidence: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  alignment: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                },\\n                required: [\'claim\', \'evidence\', \'alignment\'],\\n              },\\n              description: \'Actual achievements or project claims from the resume.\',\\n            },\\n            recommendations: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: { type: Type.STRING },\\n              description: \'Concrete, actionable steps to boost interview callback rate.\',\\n            },\\n            learningRoadmap: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  milestone: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  timeframe: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  actionItems: {\\n                    type: Type.ARRAY,\\n                    items: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  },\\n                  resourceSuggestion: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                },\\n                required: [\'milestone\', \'timeframe\', \'actionItems\', \'resourceSuggestion\'],\\n              },\\n              description: \'Actionable learning plan to close skill gaps.\',\\n            },\\n            interviewQuestions: {\\n              type: Type.ARRAY,\\n              items: {\\n                type: Type.OBJECT,\\n                properties: {\\n                  question: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  topic: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                  expectedFocus: { type: Type.STRING },\\n                },\\n                required: [\'question\', \'topic\', \'expectedFocus\'],\\n              },\\n              description: \'Realistic interview questions based on the candidate profile.\',\\n            },\\n          },\\n          required: [\\n            \'matchScore\',\\n            \'matchedSkills\',\\n            \'missingSkills\',\\n            \'resumeEvidence\',\\n            \'recommendations\',\\n            \'learningRoadmap\',\\n            \'interviewQuestions\',\\n          ],\\n        },\\n      },\\n    });\\n\\n    const responseText = response.text;\\n    if (!responseText) {\\n      throw new Error(\'Empty response received from Gemini model.\');\\n    }\\n\\n    let parsedResult;\\n    try {\\n      parsedResult = JSON.parse(responseText);\\n    } catch (parseErr) {\\n      console.error(\'Failed to parse Gemini response as JSON:\', responseText);\\n      throw new Error(\'Gemini model output could not be parsed as valid JSON.\');\\n    }\\n\\n    // Return the verified analysis data\\n    return res.status(200).json({\\n      success: true,\\n      data: parsedResult,\\n      meta: {\\n        resumeSource: resumePdfName ? `PDF: ${resumePdfName}` : \'Pasted Text\',\\n        extractedLength: finalResumeText.length,\\n        analyzedAt: new Date().toISOString(),\\n      },\\n    });\\n  } catch (error: any) {\\n    console.error(\'Error in /api/analyze-resume:\', error);\\n\\n    // Handle quota limits and specific API errors gracefully\\n    const errorMessage = error?.message || String(error);\\n\\n    if (errorMessage.includes(\'RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED\') || errorMessage.includes(\'429\')) {\\n      return res.status(429).json({\\n        error: \'Gemini API quota or rate limit exceeded. Please wait a few moments and try again.\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    if (errorMessage.includes(\'API_KEY_INVALID\') || errorMessage.includes(\'invalid api key\')) {\\n      return res.status(401).json({\\n        error: \'Invalid Gemini API key. Please check your GEMINI_API_KEY configuration in Settings > Secrets.\',\\n      });\\n    }\\n\\n    return res.status(500).json({\\n      error: `Resume analysis failed: ${error?.message || \'Unexpected server error occurred. Please try again.\'}`,\\n    });\\n  }\\n});\\n\\n// Mount Vite middleware for dev or serve dist in production\\nasync function startServer() {\\n  if (process.env.NODE_ENV === \'production\') {\\n    app.use(express.static(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\')));\\n    app.get(\'*\', (req, res) => {\\n      res.sendFile(path.resolve(__dirname, \'dist\', \'index.html\'));\\n    });\\n  } else {\\n    const { createServer } = await import(\'vite\');\\n    const vite = await createServer({\\n      server: { middlewareMode: true },\\n      appType: \'spa\',\\n    });\\n    app.use(vite.middlewares);\\n  }\\n\\n  app.listen(port, () => {\\n    console.log(`SkillBridge AI full-stack server running on port ${port}`);\\n  });\\n}\\n\\nstartServer();\\n\",\"Description\":\"Create server.ts running Express backend with Vite middleware and /api/analyze-resume Gemini endpoint\",\"Overwrite\":true,\"TargetFile\":\"/server.ts\",\"toolAction\":\"Creating server.ts\",\"toolSummary\":\"Create server.ts\"}"
      thought_signature: ""
      original_name: "write_to_file"
    }
