  planner_response {
    response: "The placeholder \"Form Staged\" flow has been removed and replaced with a real, asynchronous **Gemini API** evaluation pipeline.\n\n### Changes Implemented:\n\n1. **Full-Stack Gemini API Server Endpoint (`server.ts`)**:\n   - Built a secure backend route at `POST /api/analyze-resume` using the `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK and Express with Vite middleware.\n   - Initialized Gemini securely server-side using `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` with the required `User-Agent: \'aistudio-build\'` telemetry header.\n   - Configured `gemini-3.8-flash` with strict structured JSON schema enforcement (`responseMimeType: \"application/json\"` and `responseSchema`) to guarantee the required evaluation structure.\n\n2. **PDF Resume Text Extraction & Validation**:\n   - Implemented real PDF extraction using `pdf-parse`.\n   - When a PDF is uploaded, the server decodes the document and extracts the text layer.\n   - If the PDF has no selectable text (e.g. an un-OCRed scanned image) or is corrupted, it returns an explicit error:\n     > *\"Unable to extract readable text from the uploaded PDF. The file may be a scanned image without an OCR text layer or password-protected. Please upload a text-based PDF or paste your resume text directly.\"*\n   - Also supports pasted resume text as an alternative, validating that either a readable PDF or pasted text is provided.\n\n3. **Structured Gemini Schema**:\n   The model returns verified, structured JSON containing all required fields:\n   - `matchScore` (0\342\200\223100 integer)\n   - `matchedSkills` (with category and exact context where it was evidenced in the resume)\n   - `missingSkills` (with priority and recruiter rationale)\n   - `resumeEvidence` (claims, verified project evidence, and role alignment)\n   - `recommendations` (concrete bullet points to optimize the resume)\n   - `learningRoadmap` (actionable milestones with timeframes, tasks, and recommended resources)\n   - `interviewQuestions` (technical & behavioral questions grounded in candidate projects)\n\n4. **Interactive Results Interface (`ResumeAnalysisPage.tsx`)**:\n   - Removed the staged message and connected **\"Analyze My Match\"** to the asynchronous API.\n   - Added an animated loading state that communicates evaluation stages (*Extracting text*, *Evaluating requirements with Gemini*, *Synthesizing roadmap*).\n   - Once the response arrives, it displays the real analysis across dedicated tabs:\n     - **Overview & Evidence**: Overall match score gauge, strategic recommendations, and substantiated claims.\n     - **Skills & Gaps**: Grid of matched competencies alongside high-priority missing skills.\n     - **Learning Roadmap**: Step-by-step milestone timeline to close identified gaps.\n     - **Interview Prep**: Custom practice questions with talking points.\n   - Added options to reset, analyze another resume, or return to the **Dashboard**.\n\n5. **Error & Quota Handling**:\n   - Gracefully handles missing API keys (`503`), quota limits / `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` (`429`), unreadable PDFs (`400`), and network connection errors with dismissible UI error cards.\n\n---\n\n### Manual Configuration Step Required:\n- Ensure your **`GEMINI_API_KEY`** is configured in the AI Studio **Settings > Secrets** panel (or inside your `.env` file). The server automatically reads `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. No client-side key entry is needed."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Instructions Progress**\n\nI\'ve successfully integrated the real asynchronous Gemini API analysis function, replacing the placeholder success flow. The \"Analyze My Match\" button now triggers the actual analysis. My focus now is on what will trigger the API call, and what the flow will do with the results.\n\n\n**Implementing API Endpoint**\n\nI\'ve completed the server-side `/api/analyze-resume` POST endpoint, successfully receiving and formatting resume and job description data for the Gemini prompt. PDF parsing is implemented, with robust error handling for unreadable PDFs, including specific error messages for image-only or password-protected files. Users can also paste text. Finally, I\'m now using the `@google/genai` library with the project\'s configured secure API key for the Gemini API call.\n\n\n**Refining Result Handling**\n\nI\'ve implemented robust error handling for API failures, including quota limits and invalid responses. Parsing and rendering of the structured JSON from Gemini is working, displaying a comprehensive suite of results. I\342\200\231ve included detailed loading steps with animated indicators for each stage, reflecting the request lifecycle. I\'m satisfied that I\'m showing actual results.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The placeholder \"Form Staged\" flow has been removed and replaced with a real, asynchronous **Gemini API** evaluation pipeline.\n\n### Changes Implemented:\n\n1. **Full-Stack Gemini API Server Endpoint (`server.ts`)**:\n   - Built a secure backend route at `POST /api/analyze-resume` using the `@google/genai` TypeScript SDK and Express with Vite middleware.\n   - Initialized Gemini securely server-side using `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY` with the required `User-Agent: \'aistudio-build\'` telemetry header.\n   - Configured `gemini-3.8-flash` with strict structured JSON schema enforcement (`responseMimeType: \"application/json\"` and `responseSchema`) to guarantee the required evaluation structure.\n\n2. **PDF Resume Text Extraction & Validation**:\n   - Implemented real PDF extraction using `pdf-parse`.\n   - When a PDF is uploaded, the server decodes the document and extracts the text layer.\n   - If the PDF has no selectable text (e.g. an un-OCRed scanned image) or is corrupted, it returns an explicit error:\n     > *\"Unable to extract readable text from the uploaded PDF. The file may be a scanned image without an OCR text layer or password-protected. Please upload a text-based PDF or paste your resume text directly.\"*\n   - Also supports pasted resume text as an alternative, validating that either a readable PDF or pasted text is provided.\n\n3. **Structured Gemini Schema**:\n   The model returns verified, structured JSON containing all required fields:\n   - `matchScore` (0\342\200\223100 integer)\n   - `matchedSkills` (with category and exact context where it was evidenced in the resume)\n   - `missingSkills` (with priority and recruiter rationale)\n   - `resumeEvidence` (claims, verified project evidence, and role alignment)\n   - `recommendations` (concrete bullet points to optimize the resume)\n   - `learningRoadmap` (actionable milestones with timeframes, tasks, and recommended resources)\n   - `interviewQuestions` (technical & behavioral questions grounded in candidate projects)\n\n4. **Interactive Results Interface (`ResumeAnalysisPage.tsx`)**:\n   - Removed the staged message and connected **\"Analyze My Match\"** to the asynchronous API.\n   - Added an animated loading state that communicates evaluation stages (*Extracting text*, *Evaluating requirements with Gemini*, *Synthesizing roadmap*).\n   - Once the response arrives, it displays the real analysis across dedicated tabs:\n     - **Overview & Evidence**: Overall match score gauge, strategic recommendations, and substantiated claims.\n     - **Skills & Gaps**: Grid of matched competencies alongside high-priority missing skills.\n     - **Learning Roadmap**: Step-by-step milestone timeline to close identified gaps.\n     - **Interview Prep**: Custom practice questions with talking points.\n   - Added options to reset, analyze another resume, or return to the **Dashboard**.\n\n5. **Error & Quota Handling**:\n   - Gracefully handles missing API keys (`503`), quota limits / `RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED` (`429`), unreadable PDFs (`400`), and network connection errors with dismissible UI error cards.\n\n---\n\n### Manual Configuration Step Required:\n- Ensure your **`GEMINI_API_KEY`** is configured in the AI Studio **Settings > Secrets** panel (or inside your `.env` file). The server automatically reads `process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY`. No client-side key entry is needed."
