  planner_response {
    response: "The development server has been fixed and is now running on port 3000.\n\n### Root Causes & Fixes Applied:\n1. **CommonJS Module Import (`pdf-parse`)**:\n   - `pdf-parse` does not provide an ES Module default export, which caused Node.js to fail on startup with a `SyntaxError: The requested module \'pdf-parse\' does not provide an export named \'default\'`.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `server.ts` to load `pdf-parse` using `createRequire(import.meta.url)`.\n\n2. **Port Conflict (`EADDRINUSE: :::8080`)**:\n   - `server.ts` was falling back to `process.env.PORT || 3000`. Because the container environment defines `PORT=8080` for its internal proxy, the server attempted to bind to 8080 (which was already in use).\n   - **Fix**: Bound the Express dev server strictly to port `3000` on `0.0.0.0` as required by the AI Studio preview environment."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Applet Build Status**\n\nI\'ve got good news! Both `compile_applet` and `lint_applet` are in perfect shape - everything\'s green. The development server was throwing errors, but I\'ve addressed those issues. Specifically, I tackled the problem of `pdf-parse`, a CommonJS module with no default export within the ES modules system.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The development server has been fixed and is now running on port 3000.\n\n### Root Causes & Fixes Applied:\n1. **CommonJS Module Import (`pdf-parse`)**:\n   - `pdf-parse` does not provide an ES Module default export, which caused Node.js to fail on startup with a `SyntaxError: The requested module \'pdf-parse\' does not provide an export named \'default\'`.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `server.ts` to load `pdf-parse` using `createRequire(import.meta.url)`.\n\n2. **Port Conflict (`EADDRINUSE: :::8080`)**:\n   - `server.ts` was falling back to `process.env.PORT || 3000`. Because the container environment defines `PORT=8080` for its internal proxy, the server attempted to bind to 8080 (which was already in use).\n   - **Fix**: Bound the Express dev server strictly to port `3000` on `0.0.0.0` as required by the AI Studio preview environment."
    thinking_duration {
      nanos: 924882449
    }
