  user_input {
    user_response: "The Gemini API key has now been configured for my existing SkillBridge AI project.\n\nNow complete and test the actual AI-powered resume evaluation feature.\n\n1. Inspect the existing project and locate the \"Analyze My Match\" button and its form submission handler.\n\n2. Remove the placeholder \"Form Staged\" message and connect the button to the real Gemini API analysis function.\n\n3. Support both uploaded PDF resumes and pasted resume text. Extract the PDF text before analysis and handle unreadable files gracefully.\n\n4. Send the actual resume text and the user\'s job description to Gemini using the project\'s configured API key and secure integration mechanism. Do not hardcode or expose the key in frontend code.\n\n5. Ask Gemini to return structured JSON with:\n   - matchScore (0\342\200\223100)\n   - matchedSkills\n   - missingSkills\n   - resumeEvidence\n   - recommendations\n   - learningRoadmap\n   - interviewQuestions\n\n6. Validate the response and display the real results in the existing SkillBridge AI results page. Do not use hardcoded sample scores.\n\n7. Show a loading indicator while the analysis runs. Handle missing configuration, API errors, quota limits, and invalid responses with readable messages.\n\n8. Preserve the existing design, landing page, dashboard, and navigation. Do not rebuild the application.\n\n9. Run the app and verify the complete workflow: resume input \342\206\222 job description \342\206\222 Gemini API call \342\206\222 actual evaluation results.\n\n10. If anything prevents the workflow from working, identify the exact issue and implement the fix where possible. Tell me if I need to perform any additional manual configuration.\n\nMake the code changes now, not just a plan."
    items {
      text: "The Gemini API key has now been configured for my existing SkillBridge AI project.\n\nNow complete and test the actual AI-powered resume evaluation feature.\n\n1. Inspect the existing project and locate the \"Analyze My Match\" button and its form submission handler.\n\n2. Remove the placeholder \"Form Staged\" message and connect the button to the real Gemini API analysis function.\n\n3. Support both uploaded PDF resumes and pasted resume text. Extract the PDF text before analysis and handle unreadable files gracefully.\n\n4. Send the actual resume text and the user\'s job description to Gemini using the project\'s configured API key and secure integration mechanism. Do not hardcode or expose the key in frontend code.\n\n5. Ask Gemini to return structured JSON with:\n   - matchScore (0\342\200\223100)\n   - matchedSkills\n   - missingSkills\n   - resumeEvidence\n   - recommendations\n   - learningRoadmap\n   - interviewQuestions\n\n6. Validate the response and display the real results in the existing SkillBridge AI results page. Do not use hardcoded sample scores.\n\n7. Show a loading indicator while the analysis runs. Handle missing configuration, API errors, quota limits, and invalid responses with readable messages.\n\n8. Preserve the existing design, landing page, dashboard, and navigation. Do not rebuild the application.\n\n9. Run the app and verify the complete workflow: resume input \342\206\222 job description \342\206\222 Gemini API call \342\206\222 actual evaluation results.\n\n10. If anything prevents the workflow from working, identify the exact issue and implement the fix where possible. Tell me if I need to perform any additional manual configuration.\n\nMake the code changes now, not just a plan."
    }
  }
}
